Sorry to keep adding to this endless thread.  But I just want to make the
observation that lojban split off from loglan because one person was
deciding how things were going to be despite what the community wanted.  The
parallel draws itself.  As a member of the community, I won't accept
non-standard use of capitalization as true lojban.  Adding << as fancy
whitespace and whatnot... whatever.  But the CLL clearly states
that capitalization is for emphasis, not for marking the start of
"sentences" and proper nouns.

It's true, anybody can publish whatever they want and call it "lojban".
 That's in their power.  I could define a Luke version of lojban that shifts
every character down one (a -> b, b -> c, etc...)  But that doesn't mean
that the LLG has to accept or endorse it.

